      "entryId": "1ti-6-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The King of kings and Lord of lords \"who only hath immortality, dwelling in the light which no man can approach unto.\" Scripture never speaks of an immortal human soul. Man was created conditionally immortal (Gen 2:16-17), lost access to the tree of life through sin (Gen 3:22-24), and receives immortality only through the gospel and the bodily resurrection at the last trumpet (2 Tim 1:10; 1 Cor 15:53-54). First principle: life is in the Son; he that hath not the Son hath not life (1 John 5:12).",
      "density": 4.4286,
      "words": 88,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 39,
      "gate": "FAIL",
      "violations": [
        "39 words (max 35): \"Man was created conditionally immortal (Gen 2:16-17), lost access to the tree of life thro…\""
      ],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Genesis 2:16",
          "Genesis 3:22",
          "2 Timothy 1:10",
          "1 Corinthians 15:53",
          "1 John 5:12"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-1-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The doxology to the only wise God. First principle: the invisible immortal King receives honor — the God no man has seen or can see is made known in the visible Son.",
      "density": 2.2286,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-6-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He shall show the title in His times. First principle: the King of kings title is scheduled for display — Daniel's God of gods and Revelation's Rider converge on the same throne.",
      "density": 2.1714,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-1-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The faithful saying with the chief of sinners as exhibit A. First principle: the mission statement is personal — came, save, sinners; and the worst sinner saved is the pattern for all who believe.",
      "density": 2.1643,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-2-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The ransom testified in due time. First principle: the giving was the price — Isaiah's poured-out soul and Mark's many are the same ransom, universal in offer, testified in time.",
      "density": 2.1214,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-2-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The triple office in faith and verity. First principle: Paul's commission is sworn and specific — a teacher of the Gentiles; the Gentile thread runs through apostolic identity itself.",
      "density": 1.9821,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-6-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The charge is given in the sight of the quickening God and the confessing Christ. First principle: Christ's trial confession is the model charge — witness is expected before power, not after vindication.",
      "density": 1.8536,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-3-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God was manifest in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, seen of angels, preached to the Gentiles. First principle: incarnation, vindication, and mission are one mystery of godliness.",
      "density": 1.6714,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-4-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Spirit's explicit forecast: seducing spirits, doctrines of devils. First principle: apostasy is Spirit-foretold, not Spirit-caused — the departures are scheduled with named mechanisms.",
      "density": 1.6071,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-2-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "There is one God and one Mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus. First principle: mediation is exclusive, incarnate, and sufficient.",
      "density": 1.4321,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1ti-4-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Labor and reproach rest on the living Savior — specially of believers. First principle: the Savior-of-all claim is distributionally qualified — universal preservation, special salvation.",
